<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>ZeParty — Client Bug Resolution Summary</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11pt;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: #2D3748;
    margin: 35px 45px;
  }
  .header {
    border-bottom: 2px solid #3182CE;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 20pt;
    color: #1A365D;
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-size: 11pt;
    color: #4A5568;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .meta-box {
    background-color: #F7FAFC;
    border: 1px solid #E2E8F0;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .meta-box table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }
  .meta-box td {
    padding: 3px 6px;
  }
  .badge-resolved {
    background-color: #2F855A;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: inline-block;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  table.bugs-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  table.bugs-table th {
    background-color: #2B6CB0;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    font-size: 10pt;
    font-weight: 600;
    border: 1px solid #2B6CB0;
  }
  table.bugs-table td {
    border: 1px solid #E2E8F0;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    font-size: 10pt;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  table.bugs-table tr:nth-child(even) {
    background-color: #F8FAFC;
  }
  .bug-name {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #1A365D;
    font-size: 10.5pt;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .bug-module {
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    color: #718096;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .footer {
    margin-top: 25px;
    border-top: 1px solid #E2E8F0;
    padding-top: 10px;
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: #718096;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="header">
  <h1>ZeParty — Bug Resolution Summary</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Client Delivery Report &bull; All Reported Issues Fixed &amp; Verified</p>
</div>

<div class="meta-box">
  <table>
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 15%; font-weight: bold; color: #4A5568;">Project:</td>
      <td style="width: 35%;">ZeParty Mobile Application</td>
      <td style="width: 18%; font-weight: bold; color: #4A5568;">Delivery Date:</td>
      <td style="width: 32%;">November 3, 2026</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="font-weight: bold; color: #4A5568;">Scope:</td>
      <td>Live Party Rooms, PK Battle, Mics, Profiles &amp; SVIP</td>
      <td style="font-weight: bold; color: #4A5568;">Status:</td>
      <td><span class="badge-resolved">100% Fixed &amp; Verified</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<table class="bugs-table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 5%; text-align: center;">#</th>
      <th style="width: 26%;">Feature / Issue</th>
      <th style="width: 33%;">Problem</th>
      <th style="width: 26%;">Fixed Status</th>
      <th style="width: 10%; text-align: center;">Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">1</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Lucky Bag Banner</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Live Party Room</div>
      </td>
      <td>Banner was oversized, rendered behind the room host avatar circle, and did not auto-dismiss.</td>
      <td>Repositioned to top overlay, redesigned into a sleek floating pill with golden glow, and added 3.4-second auto-dismiss animation.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">2</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">PK Battle Viewer Sync</div>
        <div class="bug-module">PK Arena</div>
      </td>
      <td>When PK battle started, only the host saw the battle screen; viewers remained on the normal room screen.</td>
      <td>Synced real-time PK events so the room transitions instantly into the PK battle split arena for all viewers and audience members.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">3</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Removed Dummy Data in PK</div>
        <div class="bug-module">PK Arena</div>
      </td>
      <td>PK matching was showing fake dummy profiles and simulated mock broadcasters.</td>
      <td>Completely removed all dummy and mock data. PK search now exclusively searches, displays, and matches active real online broadcasters.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">4</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Guest Mic Invitation</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Microphone Seats</div>
      </td>
      <td>Tapping "Invite to Mic" from the live viewers list did not deliver the invitation to the target user.</td>
      <td>Target user ID normalized and delivered instantly via sockets. Target user gets an Accept/Decline pop-up with auto-connecting audio.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">5</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Viewer Profile Dialog</div>
        <div class="bug-module">User Profile</div>
      </td>
      <td>Tapping a viewer's avatar or username in the live room showed an error: "User profile not found".</td>
      <td>Added proper fallback checks; viewer profile card now opens instantly with complete bio, level, and stats.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">6</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Noble Username Colors</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Chat &amp; Room Seats</div>
      </td>
      <td>Noble ranks had incorrect text colors and Imperial rank lacked the special animated mixed gradient.</td>
      <td>Corrected colors (Marquis = Crimson Red, King = Royal Gold) and implemented smooth rotating blue &amp; gold gradient animation for Imperial users.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">7</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">SVIP Backpack &amp; Mic Rings</div>
        <div class="bug-module">SVIP / Inventory</div>
      </td>
      <td>SVIP avatar frames and badges were missing from the Backpack inventory and did not display on microphone seats.</td>
      <td>Added all SVIP 1–16 frames to Backpack inventory, allowed users to equip them, and rendered equipped frames on room mic seats.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">8</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">SVIP Tag &amp; Level Badges</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Profile Details</div>
      </td>
      <td>SVIP tag showed as a flat generic chip; Wealth and Charm levels lacked tiered stage graphics.</td>
      <td>Replaced with authentic golden bear SVIP badge graphic and implemented 5-stage tiered level badges.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">9</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Offline User Presence</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Live Viewers List</div>
      </td>
      <td>Users who had left the room still appeared in the viewers list and inflated the audience count.</td>
      <td>Added instant cleanup on leave/disconnect; viewer list and audience count now update accurately in real-time.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">10</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">Room Session Expiration</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Auth / Session</div>
      </td>
      <td>Switching between rooms or brief network reconnects caused session expiration and logged users out.</td>
      <td>Safeguarded token refresh logic so active login sessions remain preserved during room transitions.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">11</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">In-Room Mini Profile Levels</div>
        <div class="bug-module">Live Party Room</div>
      </td>
      <td>Opening a user's mini profile card inside a live room showed level 0 instead of their actual levels.</td>
      <td>Connected mini profile card directly to user state to accurately display Wealth and Charm levels.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold;">12</td>
      <td>
        <div class="bug-name">New User SVIP Points Leak</div>
        <div class="bug-module">SVIP / Storage</div>
      </td>
      <td>New accounts were inadvertently inheriting 1.8M SVIP points cached from previous sessions.</td>
      <td>Isolated local storage by unique user ID, completely preventing point or level leakage across accounts.</td>
      <td style="text-align: center;"><span class="badge-resolved">Resolved</span></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="footer">
  ZeParty Mobile Application &bull; Confirmed &amp; Verified Bug Resolution Summary &bull; Ready for Client Delivery
</div>

</body>
</html>
